{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863291-got-wiki","id":863291,"title":"Got Wiki?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-10T13:25:56-07:00","id":863291,"title":"Got Wiki?","content":"Were can I go and find out enough about this game to see if I want to pay for a copy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:46:43-07:00","id":863305,"title":"","content":"Right now your best bet is probably right here. What do you want to know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:48:56-07:00","id":863308,"title":"","content":"Or the free text on the Kickstarter page which is mostly up to date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:52:12-07:00","id":863312,"title":"","content":"That's gone now. There's only the original version, which has quite a few tonal differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:54:37-07:00","id":863314,"title":"","content":"Oh is it? My bad. I had no idea. I tried reading it. But eh. It was easier to wait for the book. <br /> Which I have in pod. And is beautiful. Really. Really people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11570-vasilios","name":"Vasilios","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11570_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:52:25-07:00","id":864456,"title":"","content":"What are the main splats, the equivalents of Vampire Clans, Mage trads, or C:tD Kiths?<br /> <br /> What are the main factions? Like C:tL seasonal courts or the Camarilla/Sabbat struggle.<br /> <br /> What kinds of powers? Do the power map to the type of Beast or to some other theme?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:36:55-07:00","id":864539,"title":"","content":"Ok, so your Clan equivalent are what's called families. There's five of them, each corresponding to some sort of archetypal monster. You got Anakim - Giants, Eshmaki - things that go bump in the night, Makara - sea monsters, Namtaru - nasty, creepy-crawly things and Ugallu - death from above. Each gets a Birthright power that is unique to the family, and affinity for certain Avatisms, which includes things like breathing fire, regeneration and flight.<br /> <br /> The other axis is your Hunger, but it's not really anything to do with organisation. It just determines the method by which you recharge your magic stat. You have Collectors, who hoard stuff like a dragon, Tyrants, who recharge through displays of dominance, Predators, who hunt stuff, Nemeses, who punish the guilty like Batman, and Ravagers, who break shit. The only real organisation for beasts is the Brood, which is a lot like a werewolf pack.<br /> <br /> Powers: Beasts have two main sets of powers at their disposal. You got Avatisms, which are all about projecting your monster-soul onto reality. These are all the physical powers. They also have have Nightmares, which are more mental effects, illusions and curses. Nightmares don't map to particular families, but you can make unique ones based on other supernaturals. <br /> <br /> Which brings us to the general grab-bag all beasts get. Beast is a game intended to be crossover-friendly. As such, beasts have a few powers that let them slip into non-beast games a bit easier than other splats might. First of all, they can go pretty much anywhere. Shadow, Hedge, Underworld, Astral; you name it, they can get in. They also have the ability to blend in with other supernaturals, and sort of disguise themselves as one of them at at least a casual glance. Auspex would probably get through, but they'd need to actually <i>look. </i>They can also boost the supernatural abilities of other splats. The other most notable ability is the Lair. Every beast has a sort of pocket deep in the astral called a Lair where their Horror (monster soul) lives. They can access their lair through places resonant with it, and when they do they merge with their Horror and get a bunch of bonuses. They can also drag people into their Lair with them, which allows them to go full dragon on their ass. Beasts in a brood can join all their lairs together into a communal super-lair, which has a bunch of advantages. Oh, also every Lair has a set of lair traits, which are basically environmental effects that a beast can impose on the world under certain conditions (and which they are immune to, which is useful when the trait is &quot;on fire&quot; or &quot;underwater&quot;)<br /> <br /> Think that's most of it. I'm sure people will jump in to point out anything I missed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:34:07-07:00","id":864579,"title":"","content":"It might be worth noting that Beasts have a unique dynamic with certain traits.<br /> <br /> The above mentioned Lair is also their Power Stat (Blood Potency from Vampire) and the astral lair grows with their power.<br /> <br /> Also their Fuel (Vitae) and Integrity (Humanity) stat are the same thing called Satiety, a measure of how hungry you are, which also regulates how much of a normal person you are versus your more beastly self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:41:09-07:00","id":864583,"title":"","content":"Nightmares and Atavisms normally don't need you to spend Satiety to activate, but each has a normal and enhanced effect; Nightmares grow stronger with High Satiety, and Atavisms grow stronger with low. You can also spend a Satiety dot to unleash a supercharged version of the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}